/**
 * Popular connectors with remote MCP servers of their own, which each person connects with their own account (v1's `src/extensions/popular-apps.ts`, `pim.apps/<id>`).
 * Every one lets Pim register itself at sign-in except two: Amp's takes Pim's client metadata document instead (`client: "metadata-document"`), and GitHub's is offered once the
 * deployment registers an OAuth app at github.com/settings/developers, with this Pim's `/mcp/callback/<owner>` as its callback URL (see `docs/architecture/v2-connectors.md`),
 * and sets GITHUB_CLIENT_ID and GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET. Left out, because their servers only take clients they approved: Canva, Dropbox, Figma, Ramp, Square, Vercel and Zapier.
 */
